EVALUATION.md §1, CODEGEN.md §5.6, §5.12 (log-2026-09-25, E8019 lift round 2): an input field is never decoded by a data loader, so a dependent field whose discriminant is one is DependentType at the dependent field, in both loaders.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A kind.
enum K { one, two }

/// A payload.
type P(k: K) = match k { one => Int, two => String }

/// A thing.
record Thing {
  /// Its kind, from the environment.
  k: input K from env "KIND"
  /// Its payload.
  p: P(k)
}

/// The thing.
let thing: Thing = { p: 1 }

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: data }
emit cpp { out: "@features/ac", namespace: "a", mode: data }
emit json { out: "out/" }
-- a.thing.json --
{"p": 1}
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:14:3
  emit cpp in data mode cannot generate a dependent type

error[E8019]  a/a.canon:14:3
  emit go in data mode cannot generate a dependent type

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
